At the bottom of the page where you downloaded the Nethack 3.4.3
game, you should find a link to download 32x32 tiles (the size I
usually use, there is a pretty fierce tradeoff between tile size
and screen map coverage).  There are _lots_ of nice tile sets you
can download, the top of the line is probably the "Absurd Tile Set",
the one to which I added my stealth Britney Spears as Valk tile.

That tile set goes up to 128x128, only one of the many reasons to
call it "absurd"; that one tile set is around 78 megabytes of data,
but if you can finess more than about a 6x8 view of the dungeon,
it is way splendid.

It has other sizes. edges 64, 72, 96, 128 in all, but I used scaling
with The Gimp to create additional versions at 48, 32, and 24 for my
own use.

Notice that for either choice of sets, you must make a couple of
changes to the defaults.nh options controlling text file; mine
look like this, where all the lines prefaced with "#" are just
comments; notice also that here I'm using the 48x48 set:

# Use the optional 32x32 (large) tiles that come with NetHack
# OPTIONS=tile_file:tiles32.bmp, tile_width:32, tile_height:32

# Use the optional 64x64 (small absurd) tiles
# OPTIONS=tile_file:absurd64.bmp, tile_width:64, tile_height:64

# Use an optional 48x48 (smaller absurd) tile set made with GIMP
# from the 64x64 version.
OPTIONS=tile_file:absurd48.bmp, tile_width:48, tile_height:48

# Set some options to control graphical window-port (these will
# be safely and silently ignored by the tty port)
#
# Map window settings
# possible map_mode options include:
tiles|ascii4x6|ascii6x8|ascii8x8|ascii16x8|
#
ascii7x12|ascii8x12|ascii16x12|ascii12x16|
#                                    ascii10x18|fit_to_screen
# OPTIONS=map_mode:tiles,scroll_margin:5
OPTIONS=map_mode:tiles,scroll_margin:20

